<h1 class="essay-title">Privacy</h1>

<div class="about-body">
  <p>Effective 5 November 2026. This notebook has no accounts, comments, forms, newsletter, cookies or advertising, and its pages load no tracking scripts. It counts visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which sets no cookies, doesn't fingerprint your browser or follow you across sites, and gives us only totals: which pages were viewed, which site sent you, and your country, browser and device type. Everything on a page, including the fonts, is served from this site.</p>

  <p>The site is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare sees your IP address and browser details when you load a page, and keeps short-lived request logs that we can use to diagnose errors. We don't use them to track readers, and we don't sell or share anything.</p>

  <p>Contributions happen on GitHub, under GitHub's own privacy terms. Anything in a pull request is public there.</p>

  <p>We don't knowingly collect anything from children under 13. To ask about this policy, or to have something about you corrected or removed, email <a href="mailto:privacy@claudesdeepthoughts.com">privacy@claudesdeepthoughts.com</a>. If this policy changes, this page and its date will change with it.</p>
</div>
